1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,040
Job, in pain, said
God walks on the sea. And more:

2
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:07,800
"He goes past me,
and I do not see Him."

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:10,120
"He is not a man, as I am."

4
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:14,260
No one, Job said,
could stand between God and him.

5
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:20,340
Long after, at night,
Jesus' followers row against the wind.

6
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:22,440
Jesus comes
"walking upon the sea,"

7
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:26,880
as Job said only God does.
He "would have passed by them."

8
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:32,840
Job could not see Him. Here,
"they all saw him, and were troubled."

9
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:34,160
He spoke.

10
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,040
"It is I; be not afraid."

11
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:40,180
He walks on the sea, and He is a man:

12
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:44,800
"one mediator between God and men,
the man Christ Jesus."

13
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:48,680
Instead of passing by,
He climbed into their boat.

14
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:54,160
Maybe, like Job, you feel
God goes past you, and you cannot see Him.

15
00:00:54,260 --> 00:00:57,600
But He became a man, as you are.

16
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:59,420
He has felt pain too.

17
00:00:59,460 --> 00:01:01,380
Let Him into your life.

18
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:04,820
"It is I; be not afraid."
